<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     PAGE 7-8 : ABSTRACT
     ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<h1 class="chapter">1. Abstract</h1>

<p>The <strong>Hotel Room Booking Website with Assistant Chatbot</strong> is a comprehensive, full-stack web application developed using <strong>Python</strong>, the <strong>Django 6.0</strong> web framework, and a <strong>PostgreSQL</strong> relational database. The system has been designed and developed to automate end-to-end hotel operations including room-type management, room inventory control, customer registration, online room booking with date-based availability checking, payment processing through the Razorpay payment gateway, staff administration, customer contact handling, email notifications, PDF report generation, and an intelligent assistant chatbot that can answer guest queries about rooms, bookings, staff, and hotel policies.</p>

<p>The project follows the <strong>Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC)</strong> and encompasses all the major phases: Requirements Analysis, System Design, Coding, Testing, and Documentation. It consists of eight functional modules spanning both the administrator backend and the customer-facing website, and exposes RESTful API endpoints for the chatbot and advanced search features. The application is fully responsive and works seamlessly across desktop computers, tablets, and mobile devices.</p>

<p>The administrator can manage room types, rooms, staff profiles, customer enquiries, bookings, payments, chatbot responses, and notifications from a secure backend interface. Customers can register, sign in, browse rooms by category, search with advanced filters (room type, price range, dates), book available rooms with automatic overlap detection, make secure online payments via Razorpay, interact with the chatbot for instant assistance, submit contact enquiries, and reset their passwords using email-based OTP verification.</p>

<p>The system stores data in a normalized relational database with ten interconnected tables and enforces referential integrity through primary-key and foreign-key constraints. Efficient querying, input validation, CSRF protection, and session-based access control ensure a secure and responsive user experience. The project demonstrates the practical application of RDBMS concepts, internet technology, and AI-assisted user interaction in the hospitality domain.</p>

<p><strong>Keywords:</strong> Hotel Room Booking, Django, Python, PostgreSQL, Chatbot, Razorpay, AJAX, Bootstrap, PDF Generation, Email OTP, REST API, SDLC, Software Engineering.</p>

<div class="pb"></div>

<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     PAGE 9-12 : INTRODUCTION
     ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<h1 class="chapter">2. Introduction</h1>
<h2 class="section">2.1 Background of the Problem</h2>
<p>The hospitality industry faces challenges in managing room inventory, bookings, payments, and guest communication. Many small hotels still use manual paper registers or spreadsheets, leading to duplicate bookings, inaccurate availability records, delayed communication, and difficulty generating reports. Customers increasingly expect online booking, real-time availability, and instant 24/7 support through chatbots. This project addresses these challenges with a unified web-based platform.</p>
<h2 class="section">2.2 Motivation for the Project</h2>
<p>The motivation stems from the BCSP-064 academic requirement, the real-world need for affordable hotel booking solutions, the opportunity to develop full-stack skills (Django, Python, JS, PostgreSQL), and the growing importance of chatbot-based customer service in the hospitality domain.</p>
<h2 class="section">2.3 Scope of the Project</h2>
<p>The scope covers: (1) a responsive customer-facing website with room browsing, advanced search, booking, Razorpay payment, chatbot, and OTP password reset; (2) a secure admin backend for managing room types, rooms, staff, bookings, payments, contacts, chatbot responses, and notifications; (3) a normalized PostgreSQL database with 10 tables; (4) RESTful API endpoints for chatbot, search, and notifications; and (5) PDF and HTML reporting. Multi-hotel management, dynamic pricing, loyalty programs, and OTA integration are identified as future enhancements.</p><h1 class="chapter">3. Objectives of the Project</h1>
<ol>
<li>Design a web-based hotel room booking system using Django and Python.</li>
<li>Provide responsive customer interface for browsing and searching rooms.</li>
<li>Implement date-range overlap detection to prevent double booking.</li>
<li>Integrate Razorpay payment gateway for secure online transactions.</li>
<li>Build an AI-assistant chatbot using rule-based keyword classification.</li>
<li>Implement AJAX-powered advanced room search.</li>
<li>Provide email notifications for booking confirmation and OTP password recovery.</li>
<li>Generate downloadable PDF reports of booking details.</li>
<li>Ensure secure access via authentication, CSRF, and input validation.</li>
<li>Follow SDLC practices throughout development.</li>
</ol><h1 class="chapter">4. Project Category</h1>
<p>This project spans three IGNOU categories:</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Category</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td><strong>RDBMS</strong></td><td>PostgreSQL with 10 normalized tables, foreign keys, Django ORM.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Internet Technology</strong></td><td>Full-stack Django app with HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap 5, JS/AJAX, REST APIs.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>AI Application</strong></td><td>Rule-based chatbot with keyword classification, DB queries, user ratings.</td></tr>
</table><h1 class="chapter">5. System Study</h1>
<h2 class="section">5.1 Study of the Existing System</h2>
<p>Most small and medium hotels use paper registers, phone-based reservations, or spreadsheets. These methods lack real-time availability, require manual data entry, and make reporting difficult.</p>
<h2 class="section">5.2 Limitations</h2>
<p>Double booking risk, data redundancy, slow retrieval, no online access, no automated communication, delayed payment processing, no 24/7 support.</p>
<h2 class="section">5.3 Proposed System</h2>
<p>Web-based Django application with centralized PostgreSQL database, admin CRUD, customer booking/search, Razorpay payment, chatbot, email notifications, and PDF reports.</p>
<h2 class="section">5.4 Advantages</h2>
<p>Eliminates double bookings, centralized data, AJAX search, automated reporting, session security, 24/7 online access, chatbot support, secure payments.</p><h1 class="chapter">6. Feasibility Study</h1>
<h2 class="section">6.1 Technical Feasibility</h2>
<p><strong>Conclusion:</strong> Technically feasible. Python, Django, PostgreSQL, Bootstrap, Razorpay are all mature, open-source, and within the developer's skill set.</p>
<h2 class="section">6.2 Operational Feasibility</h2>
<p><strong>Conclusion:</strong> Operationally feasible. Simple admin forms, familiar customer interface, minimal training needed, chatbot reduces staff workload.</p>
<h2 class="section">6.3 Economic Feasibility</h2>
<p><strong>Conclusion:</strong> Economically feasible. All tools are free/open-source. Only cost is web hosting (₹200-500/month). Benefits far outweigh negligible development cost.</p><h1 class="chapter">7. Tools / Platform, Hardware and Software Requirements</h1>

