<h2 class="section">11.6 Debugging and Bug Fixing</h2>
<p>Eight bugs were identified and fixed: double booking overlap logic, room type image form enctype, chatbot case-sensitivity, OTP whitespace handling, Razorpay paise conversion, staff image null handling, and search filter field mapping.</p><h1 class="chapter">12. Validations Performed</h1>
<ol>
<li><strong>Mandatory Fields:</strong> All compulsory fields must be filled.</li>
<li><strong>Password Masking:</strong> type="password" prevents shoulder-surfing.</li>
<li><strong>Numeric Validation:</strong> Price, adult/child counts accept only positive integers.</li>
<li><strong>Date Validation:</strong> Check-out must be after check-in.</li>
<li><strong>Overlap Detection:</strong> CHECKIN <= new_checkout AND CHECKOUT >= new_checkin.</li>
<li><strong>Referential Integrity:</strong> CASCADE/SET_NULL constraints prevent orphans.</li>
<li><strong>Authentication Gate:</strong> Unauthorized users redirected to login.</li>
<li><strong>Email Format:</strong> Django EmailField validates format.</li>
<li><strong>CSRF Protection:</strong> All POST forms require valid CSRF tokens.</li>
<li><strong>OTP Validation:</strong> Whitespace-stripped comparison for security.</li>
</ol><h1 class="chapter">13. Input and Output Screens</h1>
<table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Screen Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Home Page</td><td>Output</td><td>Room type category cards, navbar, chatbot widget.</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>User Sign-Up / Sign-In</td><td>Input</td><td>Registration and login forms.</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>Password Reset (3-step)</td><td>Input</td><td>Email → OTP → New password.</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>Room Categories & Filtered Rooms</td><td>Output</td><td>Cards with images, prices, Book Now.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>Advanced Search</td><td>I/O</td><td>AJAX filters + instant results.</td></tr>
<tr><td>6</td><td>Booking Form & Cart</td><td>I/O</td><td>Booking inputs + subtotal/tax/total.</td></tr>
<tr><td>7</td><td>Razorpay Payment</td><td>I/O</td><td>Card/UPI/net banking popup.</td></tr>
<tr><td>8</td><td>Chatbot Widget</td><td>I/O</td><td>Floating chat with room cards.</td></tr>
<tr><td>9</td><td>Admin Dashboard/CRUD</td><td>I/O</td><td>Sidebar, forms, data tables.</td></tr>
<tr><td>10</td><td>Admin Bookings & Payments</td><td>Output</td><td>Booking history and payment totals.</td></tr>
</table><h1 class="chapter">14. Report Generation</h1>

<p>The system generates the following reports for administrative use, customer reference, and record-keeping:</p>

<table>
  <tr><th style="width:28%">Report Name</th><th>Description</th><th>Format</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Customer Booking Report</td><td>Displays details of customers who have booked rooms including customer name, email, mobile, selected room (with room type), check-in date, check-out date, number of adults, number of children, special requests, and total price. This report helps the hotel administration track all active and past bookings.</td><td>HTML (on-screen)<br>PDF (downloadable)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Room Booking Summary Report</td><td>A summarized list of all bookings for each room showing room type, room name, booking dates, occupancy (adults + children), and total revenue per room. This report helps the hotel analyze room usage, identify popular rooms, and plan inventory.</td><td>HTML (on-screen)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Payment / Revenue Report</td><td>Payment details from the Totaldb table including customer name, mobile number, booking reference (FK), and total amount paid. This report supports financial tracking, reconciliation with Razorpay, and revenue analysis.</td><td>HTML (on-screen)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Customer Contact Report</td><td>All messages submitted through the customer contact form with customer name, email, phone, subject, and full message text. This report helps the hotel staff follow up on guest enquiries and complaints.</td><td>HTML (on-screen)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Staff Details Report</td><td>Staff information including name, designation, social media links, and photo. This report is used for internal HR records and for generating the "Our Team" section on the website.</td><td>HTML (on-screen)</td></tr>
</table>

<p>The PDF report generation uses the <code>xhtml2pdf</code> library, which converts an HTML template (rendered using Django's template engine) into a downloadable PDF document. The process involves:</p>

<ol>
  <li>Preparing the context data (booking details, customer name, etc.)</li>
  <li>Rendering an HTML template to a string using <code>render_to_string()</code></li>
  <li>Creating an HttpResponse with <code>content_type='application/pdf'</code></li>
  <li>Setting the <code>Content-Disposition</code> header for file download</li>
  <li>Calling <code>pisa.CreatePDF()</code> to convert the HTML string to PDF</li>
  <li>Returning the PDF response to the browser</li>
</ol>

